  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>More be the number of unpaired electrons <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8594;</mo></math> more be the magnetic moment.</p><p>and</p><p>Number of unpaired electrons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mg</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Number of unpaired electrons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Ti</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Number of unpaired electrons in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Number of unpaired electrons in</p><p>Thus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Fe</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> show maximum value of magnetic moment <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>)</mo></math>.</p><p>also, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt></math>.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>BM</mo></math>&nbsp;(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo></math> Number of unpaired electrons).</p>",
